#      the key's team across authenticated v1/v2 requests, constrain both
#      shared single/bulk predicates outside their ownership OR, and cover
#      Hono PDF routes plus deleteDocument's recipient self-hide fallback.
# Why-not-additive: all policy lives in the owned api-token-team-scope module.
#      The six upstream files authenticate/authorize these operations, so
#      they require narrow calls into that module. Most diff lines are the
#      existing handler arguments indented by the async scope callback;
#      no policy is duplicated into these upstream handlers. The new E2E
#      spec is declared owned at its exact Playwright-discovered path.
# Upstream-merge-fragility: high — central auth/query helpers and shadow PDF
#      routes. Preserve API-only scope on new entry points and the outer
#      team condition on every ownership branch. Human sessions must retain
#      their existing permissions. A fresh adversarial review and at least
#      two reviewers for the shared query helpers are required before merge.
# Tests: api-token-team-boundary.test.ts + api-token-team-downloads.test.ts
#      fail 14/pass 13 before implementation; all 27 pass after. The owned
#      scope unit suite checks async cleanup, nested scopes and bundle copies.
#      The owned Playwright spec uses real HTTP/PostgreSQL in the isolated
#      E2E environment; its final PR run remains required (do not watch it).

